From e893e645ba32cf888b9071d994b5f6fe7aba7177 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BankkRoll <106103625+BankkRoll@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 10:52:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs: audit JSDoc and comments across src for consistency

Port the applicable documentation audit onto current main so source comments
and editor hovers are more consistent for contributors.

- Add JSDoc to previously bare exports and non-obvious type properties covered
  by the donor audit.
- Add file-level headers and consistent section separators where applicable.
- Prefer comments that explain intent over line-by-line narration.
- Normalize em dashes to hyphens in comments and a few user-facing
  console/error strings.

The donor branch also carried an auth-settings fix and test, but current main
does not contain that parent feature; this port intentionally leaves those
deleted files out rather than resurrecting stale runtime code.

Runtime changes are limited to em-dash normalization in user-facing strings.

Verification: the build passes and 31 test files (208 tests) pass. The
external-Postgres suite and native db-reset test could not start because the
bundled PostgreSQL requires libxml2.so.2, which is unavailable on this host.
